   "s": 0,
   "loc": "Point 02 (Biggest Challenge) — Initial Phone Call…",
   "text": "[Point 02 (Biggest Challenge) — Initial Phone Call]\nStrategy: Keep the conversation light, one question at a time, and pick up on tone, hesitation, and the main concern.\nUseful questions:\n- \"So far, what's been [name]'s biggest challenge learning English, Mom?\"\n- \"Is the difficulty more with their English ability, confidence, or staying consistent?\"\n- \"Have they had a learning experience before that didn't quite fit?\"\nDig deeper: Pick one main barrier. Ask for a brief example so the concern doesn't stay abstract.\n\n### Point 02 (Biggest Challenge) — Initial Chat\n\nStrategy: Send short messages, 1–2 questions at a time, and use the customer's own words to shape your follow-up.\nUseful questions:\n- \"So far, what's the part that makes [name] struggle most, Mom?\"\n- \"Is it more about confidence, understanding English, practice, or consistency?\"\n- \"Have they learned somewhere else before? Any experience that didn't quite fit?\"\nDig deeper: Use the customer's answer as an anchor. One barrier → one follow-up → then move on to the next thing."
