   "s": 0,
   "loc": "Point 04 (How You Like to Learn) — Initial Walk-In…",
   "text": "[Point 04 (How You Like to Learn) — Initial Walk-In]\nStrategy: Ask about past learning experiences and the classroom activities that make the student enjoy learning, feel comfortable, and want to take part.\nUseful questions:\n- When you learn English, what kind of activity do you like most?\n- Are you more comfortable learning alone, in pairs, or in a group?\n- What part of class usually makes you the most excited?\nDig deeper: Explore why they enjoy that approach and connect it to their learning needs.\n\n### Point 04 (How You Like to Learn) — Initial Phone Call\n\nStrategy: Explore past learning experiences and the learning preferences that make the student more comfortable, engaged, and consistent.\nUseful questions:\n- When learning English, what kind of activity do you usually prefer?\n- Are you more comfortable learning alone or with friends?\n- What usually makes learning English feel enjoyable, or instead boring?\nDig deeper: Explore the reasons behind that preference and check whether a past learning experience shaped it.\n\n### Point 04 (How You Like to Learn) — Initial Chat"
