   "loc": "Point 05 — English Journey: YOUR ENGLISH JOURNEY — CEFR LEVELS…",
   "text": "[Point 05 — English Journey: YOUR ENGLISH JOURNEY — CEFR LEVELS]\nNeed: Place the student at a suitable starting point based on their current ability and placement results where available.\nWhy it matters: Placement isn't just a number. The result helps answer: WHERE ARE YOU NOW? → WHERE DO YOU WANT TO GO? → WHAT LEARNING JOURNEY CAN HELP YOU GET THERE?\nSignals to look for: Current level, gap against the goal, the student's response to the placement result, and questions about the starting point or target.\nWhat to avoid: Don't treat placement as a label of ability. Don't add levels/claims that aren't in the official material.\n\n### Point 05 (English Journey) — Initial Walk-In"
