   "loc": "Point 05 (English Journey) — Initial Phone Call…",
   "text": "[Point 05 (English Journey) — Initial Phone Call]\nStrategy: Keep the conversation light, one question at a time, and pick up on tone, hesitation, and the main concern.\nUseful questions:\n- \"Let me help read the placement result as a starting point, Mom.\"\n- \"Now that we know the current position, what ability are you aiming for?\"\n- \"I can briefly explain the CEFR so it's easier to picture.\"\nDig deeper: Use simple, brief language. Make sure the customer understands what the starting point means before moving on to the next part of the journey.\n\n### Point 05 (English Journey) — Initial Chat\n\nStrategy: Send short messages, 1–2 questions at a time, and use the customer's own words to shape your follow-up.\nUseful questions:\n- \"Let me help explain the placement result as [name]'s starting point, Mom.\"\n- \"From the current level, what's the most desired next target?\"\n- \"If you'd like, Mom, I can help explain the CEFR so it's easier to picture.\"\nDig deeper: Explain in 2–3 short sentences. If the customer is confused, send the explanation in steps rather than one long paragraph."
