   "loc": "Point 06 — Success Target Timeline: YOUR SUCCESS TARGET TIMELINE…",
   "text": "## Point 06 — Success Target Timeline: YOUR SUCCESS TARGET TIMELINE\n\nNeed: Determine when the student wants to see results or reach a specific English target, then understand how urgent that target is.\nWhy it matters: A timeline makes the success target more concrete and helps the advisor judge whether the target, starting point, learning journey, frequency, and schedule are realistic.\nSignals to look for: School deadlines, exams, school/university entry, competitions, travel, work/business needs, personal milestones, parent expectations, or a target without a deadline that still needs to be made more specific.\nWhat to avoid: Don't promise results within a certain time without considering the current level, target, consistency, frequency, and learning journey.\n\n### Point 06 (Success Target Timeline) — Initial Walk-In"
