   "text": "[Point 06 (Success Target Timeline) — Initial Chat]\nStrategy: Turn the customer's target into a concrete timeline by asking about the deadline, milestone, and urgency.\nUseful questions:\n- When do you want to reach this target?\n- Is there a deadline or particular moment that makes it important?\n- By that time, what do you want to be able to do in English?\nDig deeper: If the answer is still general, help turn it into a milestone that can be pictured.\n\n## Point 07 — Possible Schedule: POSSIBLE SCHEDULE\n\nNeed: Find a realistic learning schedule, not just a slot that is theoretically free.\nWhy it matters: A schedule that fits the student's and family's routine raises the chance the program can actually be carried out consistently.\nSignals to look for: Consistently free days/times, routine activities, travel time, parent availability, and possible conflicts.\nWhat to avoid: Don't just ask \"when are you free?\". Don't offer a schedule before understanding the routine.\n\n### Point 07 (Possible Schedule) — Initial Walk-In"
